<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  YARD TRADES

  What a small or middling house's own yard can take up, once it has a free cell inside its
  rect and outside its walls. First-pass set of four. Each entry is registered by Key exactly
  the way KingdomBuildings.xml entries are: a later file re-using a Key owns that trade's whole
  spec, including retheming its blueprint, its prose, or what it shades.

    DisplayName  How the founder reads it in a list.
    Blueprint    The object placed in the yard. Never a vanilla blueprint here, because vanilla
                 ships none of these; see ObjectBlueprints.xml for the four raised alongside
                 this file.
    Trade        The trade itself, as a household is said to take it up. Optional; falls back
                 to DisplayName.
    Shades       support:amount ceiling, KingdomCatalogueRules' own language. It supplies
                 nothing by itself. Non-food support needs the exact standing object's provider;
                 vine food uses the dedicated exact-fixture physical flow. Capped small on purpose
                 (KingdomYardRules.MaxShadePerWork) — a household's sideline never competes
                 with a purpose-built work.
    Goods        Yes for a trade whose output is a caravan good rather than anything the
                 settlement's own equilibrium reads. Each exact standing household adds one
                 dram to every due charter cycle, up to four households per caravan. Goods and
                 Shades are mutually exclusive. The dye vat's own case.
-->
<kingdomyardworks Schema="1">
  <yardwork Key="vinelattice" DisplayName="vine lattice" Blueprint="r_KingdomVineLattice"
            Trade="tending the vine" Shades="food:1" />
  <yardwork Key="hiderack" DisplayName="hide rack" Blueprint="r_KingdomHideRack"
            Trade="tanning" Shades="craft:1" />
  <yardwork Key="dyevat" DisplayName="dye vat" Blueprint="r_KingdomDyeVat"
            Trade="dyeing" Goods="Yes" />
  <yardwork Key="vellumpress" DisplayName="vellum press" Blueprint="r_KingdomVellumPress"
            Trade="scrivening" Shades="learning:1" />
</kingdomyardworks>
